# Extended regular expressions matched against paths inside the retained
# com.android.tethering compatibility APEX. Its framework and system-server
# classpath fragments remain for Android boot compatibility, but no executable
# network service, tethering application, BPF program, native/JNI runtime, or
# daemon init file may ship. Lines starting with "!" are permitted patterns:
# a path matching a permitted pattern is exempt from the forbidden patterns.
^bin/
^(priv-)?app/
^lib(64)?/
^etc/bpf/
^etc/.*(netbpfload|ot-daemon).*rc$
# service-connectivity compiles against this resource-only APK (no code); it
# is exempted by exact path so no other application can hide beside it.
!^priv-app/ServiceConnectivityResources@[A-Za-z0-9._-]+(/ServiceConnectivityResources\.apk)?$
